date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/JayAsker/reciting-is-not-decompressing"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JayAsker/reciting-is-not-decompressing"
abstract: >-
  A negative result on inverting LZMA2 with a byte-level transformer, written as satire.
  A 2.8M-parameter model reaches 100 percent exact match on its training set and 0 percent
  on held-out streams; a lookup table keyed on the input does the same, which is the point.
  Nothing here is peer reviewed and nothing here is a claim about the state of the art.
keywords:
